<section class="section">
  <div class="container article-body" style="max-width:920px;">
    <h2>What Makes the Dipped Cone Special</h2>
  <p>There's real theater in watching a Dipped Cone come together. As soon as the vanilla soft serve cone is swirled and turned upside down into the vat of warm dipping chocolate, the extreme temperature difference triggers instant crystallization. Within seconds, a glossy, brittle shell forms that traps the melting soft serve inside while creating an irresistible texture contrast. Explore our full spectrum of cones and novelties on <a href="/">The Queen Dairy Menu</a>.</p>

  <h2>Chocolate Dipped Cone vs. Vanilla Cone — Is the Upgrade Worth It?</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table"><thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Price</th><th>Cal</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Vanilla Soft Serve Cone (Regular)</td><td class="price-cell">$2.39</td><td>230</td><td>Clean, simple, cheapest</td></tr><tr><td>Chocolate Dipped Cone (Regular)</td><td class="price-cell">$3.19</td><td>330</td><td>Crispy shell, $0.80 upgrade</td></tr><tr><td>Crunchin' Cookie Dipped Cone</td><td class="price-cell">$3.49</td><td>350</td><td>Cookie-crunch coating, $1.10 upgrade</td></tr><tr><td>Hot Fudge Sundae</td><td class="price-cell">$3.79</td><td>300</td><td>Warm fudge in a cup, $1.40 upgrade</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

  <h2>The Shell — How It Works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>The chocolate is liquid when applied</strong> — The coating is a specially formulated dipping chocolate that remains liquid at room temperature but hardens on contact with frozen soft serve</li>
    <li><strong>It hardens within seconds</strong> — You can watch it solidify as the DQ crew dips and lifts the cone</li>
    <li><strong>It shatters on the first bite</strong> — Unlike a soft chocolate coating, the DQ dip becomes brittle and creates a satisfying crack with each bite</li>
    <li><strong>It seals the soft serve</strong> — The shell slows the melt slightly, giving you a few extra seconds before the ice cream drips</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Crunchin' Cookie Dipped Cone — The Other Upgrade</h2>
  <p>If you're eager to elevate your dipped cone experience even further, look out for the Crunchin' Cookie Dipped Cone ($3.49). Instead of a smooth shell, it embeds crunchy chocolate sandwich cookie crumbs directly into the hardened chocolate dip, adding an extra biscuit-like crunch to every mouthful. Whichever you prefer, both deliver extraordinary handheld pleasure.</p>

